// HORTULANUS'S COMMENTARY ON THE EMERALD TABLET, in the English of The Mirror
// of Alchimy (London, 1597), with the Tablet as that book prints it before the
// commentary.
//
// The text comes from hortulanus-text.ts, generated by
// scripts/texts/hortulanus-mirror.py from the Text Creation Partnership's
// transcription (EEBO-TCP A01683, keyed from the Huntington Library copy),
// compared word by word with Adam McLean's transcription and the OCRs of two
// copies, every doubtful reading settled on the page images of both copies.
// The 1597 spelling is kept; long s is printed s and abbreviations are
// expanded. There is no editorial apparatus in the book to leave out; running
// heads, page numbers, signatures and catchwords are left out.
//
// The work (arab.comm) is meant to hold several medieval commentaries; this
// stage imports one, Hortulanus's, as a treatise (arab.comm.hort) whose units
// are its thirteen chapters, with the Tablet, the prayer and the preface
// before them. The Latin (De Alchemia, Nuremberg 1541) is public domain but is
// cited, not transcribed: only one copy's images could be read. Linden's
// edition of the 1597 book (1992) is in copyright and cited only.
//
// The 1597 book is attributed to Roger Bacon on its title page, an attribution
// scholars doubt; its translator is not named. Hortulanus's date is disputed.
//
// Nothing is marked verified, and the thirteen chapters have not been checked
// against a stated inventory of the Latin (inventoryVerified stays false).

